[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852279085","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120803#issuecomment-4852279085","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120803","id":4852279085,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABITfnLQ","user":{"login":"dagarsar","id":32908423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTA4NDIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32908423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar","html_url":"https://github.com/dagarsar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T08:45:13Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T08:45:13Z","body":"Why can't it be equal to 1.0? The linked issue only mentions less than 1.0 being problematic. Is it problematic to have 1.0 values as well?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852279085/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852588847","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120803#issuecomment-4852588847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120803","id":4852588847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABITyhLw","user":{"login":"CD-DA","id":145823278,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLEWLg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145823278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA","html_url":"https://github.com/CD-DA","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CD-DA/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T09:17:05Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T09:17:05Z","body":"> Is it problematic to have 1.0 values as well?\r\n\r\n`set_zoom_step()` will eventually call a `ViewPanner`'s `set_scroll_zoom_factor()` method. That method will give an error when trying to set the zoom step to exactly 1.0: `ERR_FAIL_COND(p_scroll_zoom_factor <= 1.0)`. Honestly I think this is a bit of a bug, because looking at the code there is really no reason it shouldn't allow that","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852588847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852875666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120803#issuecomment-4852875666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120803","id":4852875666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIUEBkg","user":{"login":"dagarsar","id":32908423,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTA4NDIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32908423?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar","html_url":"https://github.com/dagarsar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dagarsar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T09:40:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T09:48:04Z","body":"Checking out the code in `ViewPanner`, it looks like there is no problem in its `scroll_zoom_factor` being `1.0`. This PR should probably fix both checks to allow for `1.0`.\r\n\r\nI think I've found a bug in `ViewPanner` though: in `gui_input`, the `scroll_zoom_factor` is used to calculate a `zoom_factor` variable that is unused, in 2 different cases. I don't know if it should be used or deleted, but I don't think it is correct. \r\n\r\nEdit: I think this `ViewPanner` unused variable should be addressed in a different issue/PR. This one should just fix both checks IMO (although a maintainer should weigh in)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4852875666/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4853209615","ht